<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hasanwayh ibn Husayn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 979</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Hasanuyeh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hasanwayh ibn Husayn was a chief of the Kurdish Barzikani tribe who founded the Hasanwayhid dynasty in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a>. From 959 he ruled the mountains around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dinavar">Dinavar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamadan">Hamadan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahavand">Nahavand</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahrizor">Shahrizor</a> under the loose overlordship of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyid-dynasty">Buyids</a>. He was praised for keeping the roads safe and for his charity, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badr-ibn-hasanwayh">Badr ibn Hasanwayh</a> continued the dynasty.</p></div>
